From 61b6363e4748852d2102a4c81fb1ac5aab4adb1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 20:03:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02426/11362] [outer-loop] tu93 deep-solves to L3 via fresh_env
 branch mode (gotcha #7)

tu93's env.reset() is NON-IDEMPOTENT: it leaves a parity-toggling hidden
state (same path, 6 reset+replays -> levels [1,2,1,2,1,2]). The reuse-one-env
'replay'/'deepcopy' OfflineSolver search therefore detected parity-contingent
L2+ "wins" that failed the fresh-env reproduction gate (correctly rejected --
no false claim), capping the tu93 adapter at L1.

The new OfflineSolver branch_mode='fresh_env' (kit change, committed prior)
evaluates every candidate on a brand-new env so each sees the same pristine
parity-0 the gate uses. The tu93 adapter now sets branch_mode='fresh_env' and
DEEP-SOLVES to L3, offline-reproduction-gated (47 actions, 5903 states,
reproduced_levels=3, per-level [18,10,19]).

- arc_loop_solve: persist the winning action path ("solution"/"solution_labels")
  so the metaharness/3rd-party can replay-gate it (ARC reproducibility discipline).
- metaharness: RESOLVED_ARTIFACTS["tu93"] -> arc_loop_solve_tu93.json (L3).
  Authoritative aggregate now 26 levels / 15 games (was 23/14): tu93 L1->L3 (+2)
  and sc25 L1 (E3 plan) counted.
- gate eval (carnot policy): 26/183 levels, 15 games, mean_eff 0.425.
- registry: tu93 levels_reproduced 2->3; general gotcha #7 (non_idempotent_reset)
  documented; totals reconciled to the metaharness.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
